<div class="sheethead">
    <span class="code mono">SHEET 02</span>
    <h1>Why IML</h1>
    <span class="kind mono">MISSION · FAQ</span>
</div>

<div class="card" style="padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;">
    <span class="eyebrow mono">/// DOC 002 — MISSION</span>
    <h1 style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Why IML</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin: 0;">A place where creative engineers and tinkerers design and solve real engineering challenges together, the kind of big project that's genuinely hard for one person to take on alone.</p>
</div>

<div class="grid g2 align-start" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
    <div>
        <span class="eyebrow mono">SEC. 01 — WHY IT EXISTS</span>
        <p style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-weight: 500; font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; color: var(--navy);">A lot of useful things never get built because they don't make financial sense to a capital investor.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--body-text);">That doesn't mean they're not worth doing, it just means nobody's funding them the normal way. IML exists for that gap, projects that are fun, useful, and worth building, even if they were never going to be profitable.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="spec">
        <div class="hd mono">OPERATING FACTS</div>
        <div class="row"><span class="k mono">Design phase</span><span class="v">Unpaid, speculative</span></div>
        <div class="row"><span class="k mono">Production drawings</span><span class="v">Paid, open to bid</span></div>
        <div class="row"><span class="k mono">Physical build</span><span class="v">Paid, open to bid</span></div>
        <div class="row"><span class="k mono">Funding</span><span class="v">Donations + sponsors</span></div>
        <div class="row"><span class="k mono">Licence</span><span class="v">Open source, always</span></div>
    </div>
</div>

<span class="eyebrow mono" style="margin-top: 1.25rem; display: block;">SEC. 02 — WHAT PARTICIPANTS GET</span>
<table class="tb">
    <thead><tr><th style="width:80px;">Terms</th><th style="width:150px;">Phase</th><th>What it means</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="pill paid">PAID</span></td><td><strong>Production drawings</strong></td><td>Once a design is ready to move toward a build, turning it into real working drawings is paid work. Teams can bid, and it can be split across more than one team to go faster and pay more people.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="pill paid">PAID</span></td><td><strong>Build phase</strong></td><td>Building the physical prototype is also paid work, funded the same way, donations and sponsorships raised by IML.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="pill plain">UNPAID</span></td><td><strong>Design phase</strong></td><td>Open to everyone, done on your own time. Design winners earn prizes funded by donations and sponsors, plus recognition and bragging rights.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="pill refined">OPEN</span></td><td><strong>Content</strong></td><td>The whole process gets documented and turned into content, for the designers involved and for anyone following along.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="pill refined">OPEN</span></td><td><strong>Points</strong></td><td>Winning designs earn points. If a design is ever monetized down the line, points could convert into stock, money, or royalties, not a promise. Treat points as bragging rights first.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<span class="eyebrow mono" style="margin-top: 1.25rem; display: block;">SEC. 03 — WHAT YOU NEED TO DO</span>
<div class="grid g3">
    <div class="card step-card"><div class="step-num mono">01</div><p>Sign up, as an individual or as a team.</p></div>
    <div class="card step-card"><div class="step-num mono">02</div><p>Design on your own time, with whatever tools and process you want.</p></div>
    <div class="card step-card"><div class="step-num mono">03</div><p>Upload your submission in the required format before the deadline.</p></div>
    <div class="card step-card"><div class="step-num mono">04</div><p>Submissions go public the moment the deadline hits, nothing is hidden.</p></div>
    <div class="card step-card"><div class="step-num mono">05</div><p>Designs get judged by a mix of AI, recruited experts, and the public.</p></div>
    <div class="card step-card"><div class="step-num mono">06</div><p>Comments and discussion happen right on the site, publicly, on every submission.</p></div>
</div>

<span class="eyebrow mono" style="margin-top: 1.25rem; display: block;">SEC. 04 — COMMON QUESTIONS</span>

<details class="faq-item">
    <summary>What is an IML Challenge?</summary>
    <p>A specific engineering problem inside a bigger project (like one component of the Hydrowheel) that's open for anyone to design a solution to.</p>
</details>
<details class="faq-item">
    <summary>Who can join?</summary>
    <p>Anyone. You don't need credentials, just a real willingness to work through a hard engineering problem with other people.</p>
</details>
<details class="faq-item">
    <summary>Do I need to already have an idea?</summary>
    <p>No. Some people show up with a concept already, others just want to improve or build on someone else's. Both are welcome.</p>
</details>
<details class="faq-item">
    <summary>Who sees my design?</summary>
    <p>Everyone, the moment the submission deadline passes. Nothing is private or exclusive, this is open source by design.</p>
</details>
<details class="faq-item">
    <summary>Do I get paid for my design?</summary>
    <p>Not for the design itself, that phase is speculative. You get paid once a design moves into production drawings or the physical build, both funded by donations and sponsorships.</p>
</details>
<details class="faq-item">
    <summary>What happens to a design that wins?</summary>
    <p>It moves toward production drawings, which teams can bid on as paid work, then toward an actual physical build, also paid.</p>
</details>
<details class="faq-item">
    <summary>Who judges the designs?</summary>
    <p>A mix of AI, recruited experts in the relevant field, and the general public.</p>
</details>
<details class="faq-item">
    <summary>What do points actually get me?</summary>
    <p>Recognition and bragging rights, guaranteed. If a design is ever monetized in future, points could convert into stock, money, or royalties, but that outcome isn't guaranteed and shouldn't be counted on.</p>
</details>
<details class="faq-item">
    <summary>Is this really open source?</summary>
    <p>Yes. Every design can be built on, reused, and improved by anyone. Nobody owns exclusive rights to a design.</p>
</details>

